{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>You shall hide them</b> — and thus: 'all who fear You — תסתירם'; and their hiding is that You hide the face from devious people." "<b>Marachasei</b> — from the stem of והרכסים לבקעה." "And some say: 'You shall hide them in secret' — that they see Your face from the strife of tongues." "And some say: in the secret of Your anger and Your wrath from them, in the strife of tongues because of the whisper of many."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "The second clause alludes to a verse (Psalm 31:20, 'תצפנם בסתר פניך'); Ibn Ezra quotes it elliptically.", 1 "The phrase והרכסים לבקעה appears to be a biblical phrase quoted as a parallel usage; possibly from 1 Kings 6 or a similar source, but the exact reference is uncertain to me.", 2 "The quotation blends elements from adjacent verses in the psalm; Ibn Ezra reports the reading without endorsing it.", 3 "These commentators apparently read the verse as a reference to divine wrath directed at enemies, not protection of the righteous."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:11.570332089Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}